{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>As the going forth</b> Three times in the Masorah: here and the other two: כצאת משה אל האהל and כצאת השמש בגבורתו. This is what they said: the face of Moses is like the face of the sun, and this is כצאת השמש בגבורתו. And likewise that which we say: one who works upon his going forth — is included in the World to Come. Meaning: he need not go forth to his work until the sun goes forth, even though he does not begin his work until after the hour the sun goes forth. For he is idle from the time the sun goes forth; what he spends going forth from his house until he arrives at the work — we do not say he must hasten to go forth so as to begin work at the sun's going forth. And this is like the going forth of slaves, who are not obligated to go forth except כצאת השמש (as the sun goes forth)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The two additional Masorah occurrences are Judges 5:5 and Psalms 19:6. The phrase 'פועל ביציאתו משל בעה\"ב' appears to be a compressed citation of a rabbinic dictum; rendered hyper-literally as given."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:51.852256362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}